{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.ConfinementNfPartialProof","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.ConfinementNfPartialProof","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Bounds.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finite.Defs"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.theorem_2_shift_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.theorem_2_shift_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-nf-partial-proof.lean#L187-L201","doc":"Theorem 2 of the partial proof: the shift decomposition.\nCONDITIONAL on Sub-lemma 2.1 (= the `HasBranchingBlockLemma` class\ninstance) and on `Theorem 3` (strong duality, which forces\n`Δ_resid = 0` since `|Δ_resid| ≤ duality_gap = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.HasBranchingBlockLemma.shift_decomp_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.HasBranchingBlockLemma.shift_decomp_bound","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-nf-partial-proof.lean#L183-L183","doc":"The pole-order bound that Sub-lemma 2.1 establishes:\nfor any `λ`, the q=0 pole order of `χ^λ(β)` is bounded by the\nmax over (μ, ν) in the LR branching of (per-component pole orders\n+ interface contribution).  Stated abstractly as a real inequality;\nconcrete instances (e.g. the AXKIA branch's torus-knot interface\nformula `α_shift(T_(p,k)) = k(p−1)`) populate this field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.HasBranchingBlockLemma.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.HasBranchingBlockLemma.mk","kind":"ctor","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-nf-partial-proof.lean#L176-L176","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.HasBranchingBlockLemma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.HasBranchingBlockLemma","kind":"class","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-nf-partial-proof.lean#L171-L185","doc":"Sub-lemma 2.1: the Hecke-branching block decomposition of an\ninterface generator's seminormal action.  The mathematical content\nis in docs/audits/2026-05-04-sub-lemma-2-1-categorical-proof.md;\nhere it is encoded as a class so Theorem 2 can take it as a\nhypothesis (AGENTS.md §3b-cond pattern). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.theorem_1_maximizer_in_active_set","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.theorem_1_maximizer_in_active_set","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-nf-partial-proof.lean#L163-L169","doc":"Theorem 1 of the partial proof: the Wedderburn maximizer lies in\nthe LP active set.  Conditional on `[HasFiniteLPDuality lp]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.complementary_slackness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.complementary_slackness","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-nf-partial-proof.lean#L156-L161","doc":"Complementary slackness theorem (class-conditional invocation).\nConditional on `[HasFiniteLPDuality lp]` per AGENTS.md §3b-cond. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.theorem_3_strong_duality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.theorem_3_strong_duality","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-nf-partial-proof.lean#L149-L154","doc":"Theorem 3 of the partial proof: duality_gap = 0 for the QOU\noperator-selection LP.  Conditional on `[HasFiniteLPDuality lp]`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:confinement-nf-partial-proof","label":"prop:confinement-nf-partial-proof","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-nf-partial-proof.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.strong_duality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.strong_duality","kind":"def","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-nf-partial-proof.lean#L142-L147","doc":"Strong duality theorem (now a class-conditional invocation).\nConditional on `[HasFiniteLPDuality lp]` per CLAUDE.md §3b-cond. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.HasFiniteLPDuality.complementary_slackness_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.HasFiniteLPDuality.complementary_slackness_holds","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-nf-partial-proof.lean#L139-L139","doc":"Complementary slackness: at the optimum, λ has tight primal\nconstraint iff `λ ∈ active_set`.\n-- Ref: [schrijver1986theory] §7.4 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.HasFiniteLPDuality.strong_duality_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.HasFiniteLPDuality.strong_duality_holds","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-nf-partial-proof.lean#L135-L135","doc":"Strong duality: for bounded + feasible LP, primal opt = dual opt.\n(Needs abstract LP duality infrastructure that does not exist in Mathlib; kept as an honest assumption for models without certificates)\n-- Ref: [schrijver1986theory] §7.2 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.HasFiniteLPDuality.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.HasFiniteLPDuality.mk","kind":"ctor","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-nf-partial-proof.lean#L131-L131","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.HasFiniteLPDuality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.HasFiniteLPDuality","kind":"class","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-nf-partial-proof.lean#L118-L140","doc":"Finite-dim LP duality (Schrijver §7.2 + §7.4): the two facts a\nQOU operator-selection LP needs from standard LP theory.  These are\n*not* QOU-specific — they hold for any bounded + feasible finite-dim\nLP.  Mathlib does not (as of writing) ship an LP-duality library;\nthis class axiomatises the two facts so the downstream theorems can\ntake them as explicit `[Instance]` hypotheses (AGENTS.md §3b-cond\npattern), making `theorem_1_…` and `theorem_3_…` rigorous-conditional\nresults awaiting a Mathlib LP-duality port.\n\nWhen Mathlib gains an LP-duality scope (cf.\n`https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/`), populate\nthis class via the appropriate Mathlib lemmas; the rest of the file\nneeds no change. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.OperatorSelectionLP.tight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.OperatorSelectionLP.tight","kind":"opaque","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-nf-partial-proof.lean#L108-L114","doc":"Predicate: the primal constraint at λ is **tight** at the\noptimum (= the constraint binds the optimum, equivalently\n`Σ_i a_{λ, i} t_i^* = b_λ`).  Concrete realisation uses the LP\ninner constraint matrix; here we expose it as an abstract Prop\nindexed by λ so theorems can be stated against it without unfolding\nthe LP details. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.OperatorSelectionLP.max_pole","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.OperatorSelectionLP.max_pole","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-nf-partial-proof.lean#L101-L106","doc":"Wedderburn-pole maximizer (= primal-optimal point).  Existence\nfollows from `lp.nonempty` (the partition lattice is inhabited) plus\nfiniteness (the objective attains its max on a finite set); we expose\na representative via the non-emptiness witness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.OperatorSelectionLP.active_set","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.OperatorSelectionLP.active_set","kind":"opaque","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-nf-partial-proof.lean#L98-L99","doc":"Active set of dual variables: λ with `y_λ* > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.OperatorSelectionLP.duality_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.OperatorSelectionLP.duality_gap","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-nf-partial-proof.lean#L94-L96","doc":"Duality gap = |primal − dual|. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.OperatorSelectionLP.dual_obj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.OperatorSelectionLP.dual_obj","kind":"opaque","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-nf-partial-proof.lean#L91-L92","doc":"Dual optimum value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.OperatorSelectionLP.primal_obj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.OperatorSelectionLP.primal_obj","kind":"opaque","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-nf-partial-proof.lean#L88-L89","doc":"Primal optimum value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.OperatorSelectionLP.feasible_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.OperatorSelectionLP.feasible_holds","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-nf-partial-proof.lean#L79-L79","doc":"Witness that the LP is feasible (the trivial primal point exists). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.OperatorSelectionLP.bounded_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.OperatorSelectionLP.bounded_holds","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-nf-partial-proof.lean#L77-L77","doc":"Witness that the LP is bounded above (Wedderburn dimension is finite,\nso all primal variables `t_λ ∈ [0, 1]` after normalisation; the objective\nachieves its max on a compact polytope). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.OperatorSelectionLP.nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.OperatorSelectionLP.nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-nf-partial-proof.lean#L73-L73","doc":"Non-emptiness: the partition lattice of `n ≥ 1` always\ncontains at least the trivial partition, so the LP has a feasible\nprimal point and a well-defined `max_pole`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.OperatorSelectionLP.finite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.OperatorSelectionLP.finite","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-nf-partial-proof.lean#L69-L69","doc":"Finite-dim hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.OperatorSelectionLP.Λ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.OperatorSelectionLP.Λ","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-nf-partial-proof.lean#L67-L67","doc":"The state space (partitions of `n`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.OperatorSelectionLP.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.OperatorSelectionLP.mk","kind":"ctor","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-nf-partial-proof.lean#L65-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.OperatorSelectionLP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementNFPartial.OperatorSelectionLP","kind":"structure","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-nf-partial-proof.lean#L37-L79","doc":"Abstract operator-selection LP: a finite-dim convex program over\nthe partition lattice of `n`.  The boundedness and feasibility\nproperties are carried abstractly; concrete realisation lives in\n`prop:operator-selection-lp`'s implementation files.\n\n**Parameterised 2026-09-13.**  `bounded` and `feasible` were *fields*\ntyped with the universe `Prop`, each with a `_holds` witness beside it —\nso an instance chose both propositions and `⟨True, True, trivial,\ntrivial⟩` satisfied them.  As parameters they are fixed by whoever\nwrites the type and are visible in every signature mentioning it.\n\nThey are parameters rather than encodings because there is nothing here\nto encode them against: the objective is `opaque primal_obj : … → ℝ`, a\nsingle real with no carried feasible set or constraint system, so\n\"bounded above\" and \"feasible\" have no statable content at this level of\nabstraction.  Inventing an objective to quantify over would be the\nauthor's call.\n\n🛑 **Two observations recorded rather than acted on.**  First, neither\n`bounded_holds` nor `feasible_holds` is consumed anywhere — not by\n`HasFiniteLPDuality`, not by `theorem_3_strong_duality`, not by\n`complementary_slackness`.  The docstring above said the structure \"uses\nonly the abstract bounded + feasible properties\"; in fact it uses\nneither.  Second, `nonempty : Nonempty Λ` already carries what its own\ndocstring calls feasibility (\"so the LP has a feasible primal point\"), so\n`feasible` may be a duplicate of a genuinely-encoded sibling.  Whether to\ndrop either is a modelling judgement about what this abstraction is for,\nso both are left in place and named here. ","signatureChunk":0}]}